ytdownloader (0.3.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Single merged Downloads list: running, paused, pending, retrying,
    completed and failed items all visible with progress bars 0-100%.
  * Completed/failed rows greyed out; pause/resume disabled, ✕ still removes.
  * Fix: completed downloads previously vanished (never shown in Finished/
    Completed section) - terminal state now refreshes the list.
  * Fix: long URLs no longer clip the progress bar, ETA and buttons off
    the row (label width no longer drives the row size hint).
  * Pending items can be paused/resumed individually from their rows.

 -- User <user@example.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0000

ytdownloader (0.2.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Invidious-style URLs accepted (inv.nadeko.net, invidious.tiekoetter.com, ...).
  * Full title shown on validation; downloads start only via explicit
    "Download now" / "Add to queue" buttons.
  * Completed downloads shown; not restored on startup.
  * Remove (✕) buttons on queued, active, and completed rows.
  * Pause all button; paused state persists across restarts.
  * Quit dialog notes auto-resume on next start; Shift+Ctrl+Q exits without prompting.
  * Help menu shows version.
  * Automatic state save (periodic + on exit) with restore on startup.

 -- User <user@example.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

ytdownloader (0.1.0-1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Initial release for Linux Mint LMDE 7 (Debian 12 bookworm).
  * Qt graphical YouTube audio/video downloader using yt-dlp.
  * Features: validation, queuing, parallel downloads, auto-retry with
    exponential backoff, completion verification, progress reporting.

